<title>NIGERIA: TOTAL SEEN GETTING ASHLAND NIGERIA RIGHTS -PAPERS.</title>
<headline>TOTAL SEEN GETTING ASHLAND NIGERIA RIGHTS -PAPERS.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Total is likely to acquire rights to Ashland oil production concessions in Nigeria which the military government revoked in June, local newspapers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Total of France has virtually sealed a deal with the government,&quot; the independent Vanguard newspaper said. The Guardian newspaper, also independent, carried the same story.</p>
<p>Officials of neither company nor the government were immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Nigeria cancelled Ashland's oil production sharing contracts in June, accusing it of transfering its interests to France's Perenco Investments S.A. without official consent.</p>
<p>Ashland was producing around 20,000 barrels of crude per day from its concessions in the Niger Delta before the contracts were revoked.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317</p>
